WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.334 --> 00:00:15.908
Peter pleaded with Wendy to come with him to Neverland.

2
00:00:15.909 --> 00:00:20.897
"I'll teach you to fly, and then we can fly there together," he said.

3
00:00:20.898 --> 00:00:25.252
"There are mermaids there too! Have you ever seen a mermaid?"

4
00:00:25.253 --> 00:00:28.855
"Mermaids!" cried Wendy.

5
00:00:28.856 --> 00:00:36.095
She was very excited about going, but she was worried about leaving the rest of her family.

6
00:00:36.096 --> 00:00:41.262
"You can tell the Lost Boys and me lots of stories," begged Peter.

7
00:00:41.263 --> 00:00:43.980
"Then you can tuck us into bed at night.

8
00:00:43.981 --> 00:00:47.132
None of us has ever been tucked in before.

9
00:00:47.133 --> 00:00:50.360
You can sew and make pockets for us.

10
00:00:50.361 --> 00:00:54.170
You see, none of our clothing has any pockets.

11
00:00:54.171 --> 00:00:58.407
We really could use a girl in Neverland, Wendy."

12
00:00:58.408 --> 00:01:02.704
Wendy loved the idea of taking care of Peter and his Lost Boys.

13
00:01:02.705 --> 00:01:06.393
Bravely, she tried to give him a kiss on his cheek again.

14
00:01:06.394 --> 00:01:10.742
But when she bent over to kiss him, she suddenly screamed with pain.

15
00:01:10.743 --> 00:01:15.658
"It feels as if someone is pinching me," she cried.

16
00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:18.713
"That must be Tink," said Peter.

17
00:01:18.714 --> 00:01:23.034
"I never saw her act so naughtily with a stranger before."

18
00:01:23.035 --> 00:01:27.038
Tinker Bell darted around the room.

19
00:01:27.039 --> 00:01:31.796
"She says she will pinch you again each time you do that," Peter said.

20
00:01:31.797 --> 00:01:35.625
He could not understand why, but Wendy understood.

21
00:01:35.626 --> 00:01:37.942
Tinker Bell was jealous!

22
00:01:37.943 --> 00:01:43.189
Wendy changed the subject. "Can you teach John and Michael to fly, too?"

23
00:01:43.190 --> 00:01:46.074
"If you like," Peter answered.

24
00:01:46.075 --> 00:01:50.954
For Wendy's sake, he was willing to put up with her brothers.

25
00:01:50.955 --> 00:01:54.919
Wendy shook her brothers, who were still asleep in their beds.

26
00:01:54.920 --> 00:02:01.616
"Wake up, John! Wake up, Michael! Peter is here, and he is going to teach us to fly."

27
00:02:01.617 --> 00:02:04.490
The boys got up, excited.

28
00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:11.357
"Can Peter really fly?" John asked, as he put on the black top hat he liked to wear.

29
00:02:11.358 --> 00:02:16.273
Peter didn't say anything. He just flew around the room gracefully.

30
00:02:16.274 --> 00:02:18.740
It looked so easy.

31
00:02:18.741 --> 00:02:21.815
"How do you do it?" asked John.

32
00:02:21.816 --> 00:02:25.551
He jumped off the bed and landed on his backside.

33
00:02:25.552 --> 00:02:32.138
"You just think wonderful thoughts," Peter explained, "and they lift you up in the air."

34
00:02:32.139 --> 00:02:37.894
But what Peter didn't say was that people can't fly unless fairy dust has been blown on them.

35
00:02:37.895 --> 00:02:43.325
Fortunately, Peter still had some fairy dust on his hands from Tinker Bell.

36
00:02:43.326 --> 00:02:47.347
He blew some magic dust on each of the children.

37
00:02:47.348 --> 00:02:52.551
"Just wiggle your shoulders and think lovely thoughts," he instructed.

38
00:02:52.552 --> 00:02:57.030
Michael was first, and immediately he floated up in the air.

39
00:02:57.031 --> 00:03:01.584
"Look at me, I'm flying!" he shouted.

40
00:03:01.585 --> 00:03:04.257
Then John and Wendy tried it.

41
00:03:04.258 --> 00:03:09.510
They were not as graceful as Peter, but each was able to fly across the room.

42
00:03:09.511 --> 00:03:12.399
Their heads bobbed against the ceiling.

43
00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.218
John had to hold onto his hat to keep it from being knocked off.

44
00:03:16.219 --> 00:03:20.034
Up and down they went, and round and round.

45
00:03:20.035 --> 00:03:25.189
"With a little more practice, you'll be able to fly with me to Neverland.

46
00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:31.411
You'll see the pirates and wild animals!" said Peter, tempting the boys.

47
00:03:31.412 --> 00:03:35.268
"Hooray—pirates!" cried John.

48
00:03:35.269 --> 00:03:42.602
"Hooray—wild animals!" shouted Michael.

49
00:03:42.603 --> 00:03:47.952
Meanwhile Nana, who was tied up in the backyard, kept barking.

50
00:03:47.953 --> 00:03:52.336
Liza, the servant, was preparing pudding in the kitchen.

51
00:03:52.337 --> 00:03:57.148
She was getting very annoyed; Nana had been barking all night.

52
00:03:57.149 --> 00:04:00.097
Liza stepped outside to check on her.

53
00:04:00.098 --> 00:04:08.318
"If you don't stop barking, I will have to fetch the master and mistress at Number 27," scolded Liza.

54
00:04:08.319 --> 00:04:12.133
"I'll bring them home from the party to punish you."

55
00:04:12.134 --> 00:04:17.174
This gave Nana an idea. She would get the Darlings herself!

56
00:04:17.175 --> 00:04:20.910
The dog quieted down on purpose.

57
00:04:20.911 --> 00:04:26.456
Then, when Liza returned to the kitchen, Nana pulled at her chain hard.

58
00:04:26.457 --> 00:04:29.851
It broke in two.

59
00:04:29.852 --> 00:04:35.687
She burst out of the yard, crossed the street, and ran into Number 27.

60
00:04:35.688 --> 00:04:40.079
Once she was inside, she waved her paws in the air.

61
00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:45.920
Now Mr. and Mrs. Darling knew that something terrible was happening at their house.

62
00:04:45.921 --> 00:04:50.780
Without saying good-bye to their hostess, they rushed into the street.

63
00:04:50.781 --> 00:04:56.767
When they reached their house, they looked up and saw the nursery's open window.

64
00:04:56.768 --> 00:05:11.238
By the time Mr. and Mrs. Darling ran up to the nursery, the children—Wendy, John, and Michael—had flown away with Peter.
